{"entryId":"1528","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1528:1","sourceSha256":"cc4d843b8177c39f2e68a2479d1a2cae38deee5f3602a8e04ad4818813b944f5","englishSha256":"de9e50e66786eaa4eada05a12cff755956ad7c191d4ecda786b10cda87853720","citations":[{"id":"1528:1:citation-01","he":[9,39],"en":[14,73],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_9b.12"},"reference":"Eruvin 9b:12","assessment":"Eruvin directly reverses the source’s apparent direction: Adda bar Avimi recites before Chanina. The reciprocal Heilprin entry has Adda reciting before Chananyah and gives the additional Chanina patronymic reading.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 210:1","target":{"entry":210,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Eruvin 9b:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_9b.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"The received text makes Chananyah teach before Adda. Eruvin and the reciprocal entry give Adda as reciter. The checked Eruvin uses Chanina.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 210:1","target":{"entry":210,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Eruvin 9b:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_9b.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
